---
/**
 * The claim.
 *
 * Answers one question and no other: what did Goedel say, and is it true?
 *
 * The prose is `eli5.md` from the repository root, rendered. It is not copied
 * here. If this page needs a new sentence, the sentence goes into `eli5.md`,
 * because the alternative is two tellings of the same story that drift apart --
 * which is exactly the failure `data/facts.json` exists to prevent for values.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Scoreboard from '../components/Scoreboard.astro';
import MarginNote from '../components/MarginNote.astro';
import Value from '../components/Value.astro';
import { fact } from '../lib/facts';
import { readSections, pick, render } from '../lib/content';

const eli5 = readSections('eli5.md');
const [story, meaning] = pick(eli5, 'the-story', 'what-loophole-means-here');

const memo = fact('godel.memo.quote');
const doubt = fact('godel.memo.doubt');
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<Base
  title="Gödel’s Loophole"
  description="In 1947 Kurt Gödel said the United States Constitution contained a lawful path to dictatorship. He never wrote it down. This is a machine-checked attempt to find it, and an honest account of not having found it."
  section="claim"
>
  <div class="page">
    <div class="wide lede">
      <p class="kicker smallcaps">Trenton, New Jersey &#183; <Value id="godel.exam.date" bare /></p>
      <h1>
        The greatest logician who ever lived said the Constitution
        could be used, lawfully, to end itself.
      </h1>
      <p class="standfirst">
        He gave no details. He never wrote it down. The only witness typed it up
        twenty&#8209;four years later from memory and said he did not think G&#246;del was right.
        This is an attempt to find the hole anyway &#8212; by reading the words, and by
        treating the document as a machine &#8212; with every step checked by something
        other than a person who wanted it to be true.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="wide">
      <Scoreboard />
    </div>

    <p class="verdict">
      <strong>No lawful path has been found.</strong> That is the current state of this
      project and the most useful thing on this page. What follows is what was looked for,
      how, and what turned up instead &#8212; including
      <a href={`${base}/method#disproved`}>the claims we made and then broke ourselves</a>.
    </p>

    <MarginNote head="Status" facts={['scoreboard.loopholes', 'cascade.status']} />

    <section id="story" aria-labelledby="story-head">
      <h2 id="story-head">{story.title}</h2>
      <div class="prose" set:html={story.html} />
    </section>

    <MarginNote head="The only record" facts={['godel.memo.date', 'godel.memo.doubt']}>
      <p class="pull">
        The memorandum is the entire evidentiary basis for the claim. It is a
        recollection, dictated from memory, by a man who opens by admitting he had
        not checked his diaries and closes by doubting the thing he is reporting.
      </p>
    </MarginNote>

    <figure class="memo">
      <blockquote class="document" cite="Morgenstern memorandum">
        <p>&#8220;{memo.value}&#8221;</p>
      </blockquote>
      <figcaption>
        Oskar Morgenstern, <cite>History of the Naturalization of Kurt G&#246;del</cite>,
        dictated <Value id="godel.memo.date" bare />. Four paragraphs later he adds that
        {' '}{doubt.value}.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section id="meaning" aria-labelledby="meaning-head">
      <h2 id="meaning-head">{meaning.title}</h2>
      <div class="prose" set:html={meaning.html} />
    </section>

    <MarginNote head="Why this is the hard version">
      <p>
        A coup is not a loophole and is not interesting. The claim only has force if
        every step is one the rulebook plainly allows, because then enforcing the rules
        harder is no defence &#8212; enforcing the rules is what the attacker is doing.
      </p>
    </MarginNote>

    <nav class="next wide" aria-label="Continue">
      <h2>Where to go next</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <a href={`${base}/precedents`}>
            <span class="next-label">The precedents</span>
            <span class="next-gloss">
              Three constitutions have actually died this way, and each died through a
              different layer of law. That is why the question is not silly.
            </span>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href={`${base}/text`}>
            <span class="next-label">The text</span>
            <span class="next-gloss">
              An unstated denominator in Article&nbsp;V, a corrupted First Amendment, and
              twelve places the Constitution says nothing at all.
            </span>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href={`${base}/machine`}>
            <span class="next-label">The machine</span>
            <span class="next-gloss">
              Somebody already published a formal proof of G&#246;del&#8217;s claim. It reproduces.
              It also skips the hard part, and here is exactly which part.
            </span>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href={`${base}/method`}>
            <span class="next-label">The method</span>
            <span class="next-gloss">
              The rules that make this different from confident, plausible, generated
              analysis &#8212; and the list of things we got wrong.
            </span>
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .lede {
    padding-block: var(--space-2xl) var(--space-xl);
  }

  .kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-machine);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  h1 {
    max-width: 20ch;
    font-size: clamp(var(--text-xl), 5.2vw, var(--text-3xl));
  }

  .standfirst {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    max-width: 52ch;
  }

  .verdict {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
  }

  .verdict strong {
    color: var(--disproved);
  }

  section {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }

  section h2 {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .memo {
    margin-top: var(--space-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .memo blockquote {
    border-left-width: 2px;
  }

  .memo figcaption {
    font-family: var(--font-machine);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    margin-top: var(--space-xs);
    padding-left: calc(var(--space-md) + 2px);
  }

  .pull {
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  .next {
    margin-top: var(--space-2xl);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-strong);
    padding-top: var(--space-md);
  }

  .next h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-machine);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .next ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 48rem) {
    .next ul {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
      column-gap: var(--space-lg);
    }
  }

  .next li {
    margin-top: 0;
    border-bottom: var(--border-hair);
  }

  .next a {
    display: block;
    padding-block: var(--space-sm);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .next-label {
    display: block;
    font-size: var(--text-md);
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
    line-height: var(--leading-tight);
  }

  .next a:hover .next-label {
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
    text-underline-offset: 0.16em;
  }

  .next-gloss {
    display: block;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    line-height: var(--leading-snug);
    margin-top: 0.25em;
  }
</style>
